# iterative thinking — what the click would refuse is not retried: the button is offered, the click refuses
#
# The wolf in the Test Den is an enemy in the same area, so UnderThreatImpossibleRule refuses any act
# that is not about facing it (unless the means is discreet). That is an action rule, the click's: a
# thinking retries only what is refused before the click (the willingness and choice rules), so even
# with a retry left (pineal_gland=1) "examine the wolf" is offered as a button, and clicking it gives
# the threat's refusal.
#
# Woodcraft is pinned as the means (it observes, and is not discreet).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Den" --period noon --observe-only wolf --grant-mm woodcraft --means-only woodcraft --organs pineal_gland=1

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect wolf

strategy succeed
goal examine
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect-not That will not do, and I think again
expect [Woodcraft
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect while under the threat of
quit
